Comment (policies/compliance_framework/elbv2_target_movement_restrictions.rego:8):
**Low — metric ID looks mis-mapped.**

`ACM_TLS_ENDPOINTS` refers to AWS Certificate Manager / TLS endpoint coverage, but this policy enforces a target-group protocol/port allow-list — there is no certificate dimension in the check. The controls (`ctrl-cc6-7-002`, `ctrl-cc6-7-005`) read like network movement / segmentation controls, which doesn't match an ACM metric either.

Could you confirm this isn't a copy/paste from another policy? If it is, picking a metric ID that actually reflects "approved network movement / segmentation" would make downstream dashboards roll up correctly.
