Comment (policies/compliance_framework/elbv2_health_check_configured_test.rego:78):
**Low — missing boundary and missing-field tests.**

The threshold tests cover "well past the bound" (`healthy_threshold_count: 1` vs min 2, `unhealthy_threshold_count: 11` vs max 10) but never the boundary itself:

- `healthy_threshold_count == min_healthy` (i.e. 2) should pass — currently untested.
- `unhealthy_threshold_count == max_unhealthy` (i.e. 10) should pass — currently untested.

The comparisons are `<` / `>`, so the boundaries should pass today, but adding one assertion per bound locks that in against future off-by-one drift.

Also related to the Medium on `elbv2_health_check_configured.rego:41`: there's no test that exercises the "config omits `healthy_threshold_count` entirely" case — which currently *does* fire a violation by accident of the `object.get(..., 0)` default. Whichever way you resolve that finding, a test pinning the chosen behavior would help.
